"""Build B3 static report from saved descriptor-only matches."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def main():
    d=json.loads((ROOT/'measurements.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));records=d['records']
    total=sum(r['ratio_matches'] for r in records);mutual=sum(r['mutual_ratio_matches'] for r in records)
    counts=''.join(f'<tr><td><a href="#pair-{r["pair"]}">{r["pair"].replace("_"," → ")}</a></td><td>{r["threshold_counts"]["0.6"]}</td><td>{r["ratio_matches"]}</td><td>{r["threshold_counts"]["0.8"]}</td><td>{r["mutual_ratio_matches"]}</td></tr>' for r in records)
    sections=[]
    for r in records:
        pair=r['pair'];n,m=pair.split('_');examples='; '.join(f'{e["selection"]}: source row {e["source_row"]}' for e in r['example_queries'])
        sections.append(f'''<section class="report-section pair-case" id="pair-{pair}"><p class="eyebrow">{n} → {m} · 500 valid descriptors per image</p><h2>{r['ratio_matches']} ratio matches.<br>{r['mutual_ratio_matches']} also mutual.</h2><figure class="result-figure"><a href="figures/{pair}_all_matches.jpg"><img src="figures/{pair}_matches.jpg" alt="Descriptor-only matches between IMG {n} and IMG {m}" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Left: source. Right: target. Cyan: ratio-pass and mutual. Orange: ratio-pass only. {len(r['shown_source_rows'])} lines sampled across the ratio-ranked {r['ratio_matches']} ratio passes. Open for all lines; colors do not indicate correctness.</figcaption></figure><p>The {r['ratio_matches']} source-query matches point to {r['unique_ratio_targets']} distinct target rows. Many-to-one matches are retained; mutuality is flagged separately.</p><figure class="result-figure"><a href="figures/{pair}_examples.jpg"><img src="figures/{pair}_examples.jpg" alt="Source, nearest and second-nearest feature contexts and normalized descriptors, including accepted and rejected ratios" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Each row shows source, nearest and second-nearest candidates: 40 × 40 RGB crops enlarged 4× and 8 × 8 descriptors enlarged 20×. Display uses [−3, +3]; distances use unclipped float64. RGB crops are context, not the exact grayscale sampling grid.</figcaption></figure><p>Ratio-ranked examples: {examples}. A low ratio indicates a distinctive match, but does not guarantee geometric correctness. Rejected near-threshold matches may still look plausible.</p><p><a href="data/{pair}.npz">All query arrays and accepted correspondences (NPZ)</a> · <a href="data/{pair}.json">All 500 query audit records (JSON)</a> · <a href="figures/{pair}_all_matches.jpg">All accepted match lines</a> · <a href="../B1/working/IMG_{n}.png">Source working image</a> · <a href="../B1/working/IMG_{m}.png">Target working image</a></p></section>''')
    page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>B.3 · Match the Features</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../A3/page.css"></head><body class="report-page"><main class="shell">
<header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html">Stitching Photo<br>Mosaics</a><nav class="header-nav" aria-label="B.3 navigation"><a href="../index.html">Project home <span>01</span></a><a href="#method">Nearest &amp; second <span>02</span></a><a href="#results">Six image pairs <span>03</span></a></nav></header>
<section class="project-hero"><p class="eyebrow">SYDE 671 · Assignment 3 · James Xie</p><h1>B.3 / MATCH<br>THE FEATURES.</h1><p class="project-deck">A close neighbor is a candidate. A distinctive neighbor is a better candidate.</p><div class="project-hero-rule"><span>Part B · Descriptor matching</span><span>6 adjacent pairs · {total} ratio matches</span></div></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>01 / Connect similar local descriptions.</h2><figure class="result-figure"><a href="#pair-8446_8447"><img src="figures/8446_8447_matches.jpg" alt="Feature matching across adjacent building photographs" loading="eager"></a><figcaption>IMG_8446 → IMG_8447. Displayed correspondences come exclusively from B.2 descriptor distances. Neither image coordinates nor the A.2 homographies guide matching.</figcaption></figure><p>Seven photographs form six adjacent pairs: 8443 → 8444 → 8445 → 8446 → 8447 → 8448 → 8450. Each image has 500 valid descriptors. Match forward between neighbors; reverse nearest neighbors supply the mutual flag.</p></section>
<section class="report-section" id="method"><h2>02 / Two neighbors, one ratio.</h2><p>For each valid source, sum 64 squared component differences to each valid target, then take the square root. Exact search uses blocks of 64 queries, without a built-in matcher.</p><div class="formula">D²(i,j) = Σₖ (descriptorᵢ[k] − descriptorⱼ[k])²
d₁ = nearest Euclidean distance
d₂ = second-nearest Euclidean distance, to a distinct target row
accept when d₁ / d₂ &lt; 0.7</div><p>The ratio compares the best candidate with its nearest competitor, following section 5 and figure 6b of <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2005/06/cvpr05.pdf">Brown, Szeliski &amp; Winder (2005)</a>. The Euclidean threshold 0.7 is our implementation choice.</p><p>The paper plots squared error ratios. Our Euclidean threshold 0.7 equals 0.49 for squared distances. Both ratios are saved; their thresholds are not interchangeable.</p><p>Invalid rows are excluded; distance ties use ascending B.2 row. Zero second distance rejects 0/0, while a unique zero first distance can pass. At least two valid targets are required; the threshold is strict.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>03 / Mutual is a flag, not geometry.</h2><p>A match is mutual if the target returns to the same nearest source. Reverse search uses all valid sources, without a reverse ratio test.</p><p>All forward ratio passes are retained. Of {total} accepted query pairs, {mutual} are also mutual nearest. Mutuality is a separate flag. Ratio matches can be many-to-one, and mutual matches can still be wrong.</p><p>No geometry or manual labels filter these matches. A.2 data is hash-checked only; B.4 verifies geometry.</p></section>
<section class="report-section" id="results"><h2>04 / Six pairs, one fixed main threshold.</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Ratio &lt; 0.6</th><th>Main &lt; 0.7</th><th>Ratio &lt; 0.8</th><th>Main + mutual</th></tr></thead><tbody>{counts}</tbody></table></div><p>Counts measure acceptance, not correctness or RANSAC inliers. All pairs use 0.7; 0.6 and 0.8 show threshold sensitivity.</p><p>Overviews show up to 60 ratio-ranked matches, not hand-picked correct ones. Full figures and all 500 query records are linked. Repetition, viewpoint changes and reflections can still cause errors.</p></section>
{''.join(sections)}
<section class="report-section"><h2>05 / Auditable rows for robust geometry.</h2><p>Query records retain IDs, coordinates, both neighbors, distances, ratios and flags. JSON uses null for unavailable values; NPZ uses NaN and −1 for missing values and indices.</p><p>NPZ also saves accepted IDs, candidate indices and coordinates in source-row order. Mutual flags join by source row. B.4 uses these records for geometry.</p><p><a href="measurements.json">Measurements and input hashes</a> record settings, counts and displayed rows. Upstream inputs are unchanged.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>Reproduce &amp; inspect.</h2><pre>python run_matching.py
python build_report.py
python -m unittest test_matching -v</pre><p>Run from B3 using the existing NumPy/Pillow environment. No dependency was added.</p><p><a href="matching.py">Exact neighbors, ratio test and mutual flag</a> · <a href="run_matching.py">Six-pair experiment</a> · <a href="test_matching.py">Seven analytical unit checks</a> · <a href="measurements.json">Parameters, counts and provenance</a> · <a href="../B2/report.html">B.2 descriptors</a></p><p>Checks cover known neighbors, ratios, ties, zero distances, row mapping and invalid inputs. Real checks recompute 20 queries per pair and verify ratios and hashes.</p><p class="method-note">B.4 uses RANSAC and produces one automatic mosaic with seven images, above the minimum of three.</p></section>
<nav class="project-home-nav" aria-label="Project navigation"><a class="solid-link" href="../index.html"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>Back to Project Home</a></nav>
<footer class="site-footer"><span>SYDE 671 · Assignment 3 · James Xie</span><span>B.3 · Descriptor feature matching</span></footer></main></body></html>'''
    (ROOT/'report.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
    (ROOT/'README.md').write_text(f'''# B.3 - Descriptor matching

Open report.html. Six adjacent pairs from8443,8444,8445,8446,8447,8448,8450. Current primary Euclidean d1/d2<0.7 gives{total} tentative matches;{mutual} additionally satisfy mutual-nearest consistency. These are not geometric inliers or a measured correctness rate.

matching.py performs exact float64 direct squared-difference search with64-query blocks and stable target-row ties. Invalid descriptors are excluded; second neighbor is a distinct target row. Zero-second-distance0/0 rejects; fewer than2 valid targets yields no ratio match. Euclidean ratio and squared-distance ratio are both saved;0.7 Euclidean is mathematically0.49 squared. Reverse-nearest flags use all valid sources, without reverse ratio filtering.

data/*.npz stores every source-query audit array and all ratio-pass row pairs/feature IDs/candidate indices/working and original coordinates. Match arrays follow ascending source row; query mutual flags join by match_source_rows. data/*.json contains all500 query metadata records per pair. Figure overviews show up to60 ranks spread across the ratio-ordered accepted set; full accepted-line images are separate. Local examples use lowest/median/highest accepted ratios and lowest rejected ratio, without geometry labels.

Run from B3:
```powershell
python run_matching.py
python build_report.py
python -m unittest test_matching -v
```

Seven analytical unit tests passed. Actual generation checks20 direct scalar neighbor lists per pair, squared/Euclidean ratio consistency and unchanged upstream hashes. No A2 H guides matching; no RANSAC, automatic mosaic, new dependency or publishing. B4 remains upcoming.
''',encoding='utf-8')
    print('B3 report built:',total,'ratio matches;',mutual,'also mutual.')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
